{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>נוגי</b> — nif'al form from the root יגון, and its meaning is: those grieved over the appointed place of Israel's gathering at the appointed times, like 'all the appointed times of El are consumed in the land' [Lamentations 1:4], and 'behold I have gathered them to you' [Zephaniah 3:18], for they were yours and the meaning refers to their fathers." "<b>משאת</b> — for they bore reproach upon Jerusalem; therefore it is feminine upon it."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The phrase ממועד מקום התחברות is read as 'from the appointed place of gathering'; the initial mem on ממועד may indicate the construct chain rather than the preposition."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:33.266459139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}